{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "The Capabilities Framework will use three separate capability maps (root channel, application, orderer) as specified, with only the V1.1 capability defined per map for the v1.1 release to minimize capability proliferation.",
    "For v1.1, binaries that do not support required channel capabilities will crash immediately on startup or config update, with no graceful fallback, to ensure data integrity and provide clear administrative feedback.",
    "The orderer will enforce that orderer group capabilities are enabled before application group capabilities can be enabled, to prevent blockchain forks during the initial v1.1 upgrade.",
    "The RYW (Read Your Writes) feature will be implemented via a new GetTrxState method in the chaincode shim, with per-transaction enablement, and will be limited to CouchDB state database due to LevelDB's lack of support for uncommitted transactional reads.",
    "MSPConfig will be converted to an interface with a default implementation that preserves existing configtxgen behavior, to avoid breaking existing tooling while enabling custom config generation.",
    "Chaincode singletons will be refactored to instance-scoped without changes to the public chaincode shim API, to preserve backward compatibility for existing chaincode.",
    "The test config generator for peer core.yaml and orderer.yaml will use a World struct in the existing Fabric test framework, with no changes to production config parsing logic.",
    "The new lifecycle validation interface will include a special case for the +lifecycle system chaincode to return a default majority endorsement policy, with a stub for future support of channel config policies as endorsement policies."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "All existing Hyperledger Fabric component codebases (peer, orderer, SDK, CA) and CI/CD pipelines are available in the development environment, with no need for custom environment setup beyond standard onboarding.",
    "The Capabilities Framework changes will integrate with existing channel config update processing logic, with no need to rewrite core config transaction handling from scratch.",
    "The RYW feature is only required to work with CouchDB state database for the v1.1 release, as LevelDB support is not a requirement for this increment.",
    "The org addition training materials (video and guide) are targeted at Fabric network administrators with basic familiarity with Fabric configuration and config transactions, so no beginner-level content is required.",
    "CouchDB performance testing will be conducted on a single-node CouchDB deployment, which is the most common configuration for small to medium Fabric networks.",
    "The existing configtxgen tool will continue to use the default MSPConfig implementation, so no changes to configtxgen functionality are required beyond updating it to use the new interface.",
    "The removal of chaincode singletons will not alter the external behavior of chaincode deployment, invocation, or the public chaincode shim API, only internal implementation and testability.",
    "The World test config struct will be added to the existing Fabric test framework, with all existing test configuration parameters mapped to its fields, and no changes to production configuration code.",
    "The new lifecycle validation interface will be implemented only for the new lifecycle system, with no changes required to the existing v1.0 lifecycle system."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Define Capabilities Framework Channel Config Structures",
      "activity_description": "Update channel configuration protobuf definitions to add root, application, and orderer capability maps; update config parsing code to support the new structures.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Implement Capability Validation Logic for Peers and Orderers",
      "activity_description": "Add validation in peer and orderer startup and config update processing to check if the binary supports required channel capabilities; enforce immediate crash for unsupported capabilities as per v1.1 spec.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Implement Orderer Capability Enforcement to Prevent Fork",
      "activity_description": "Add validation in orderer config update processing to ensure orderer group capabilities are enabled before application group capabilities can be enabled, to prevent blockchain forks during initial v1.1 upgrade.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Gate Existing Breaking Changes with V1.1 Capability",
      "activity_description": "Audit all existing non-backwards compatible changes in the Fabric codebase; add V1.1 capability gating to each change; link changes to FAB-6000 (crash-only breaks) or FAB-5999 (non-deterministic breaks) as required.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Develop Capabilities Framework Test Suite",
      "activity_description": "Write unit and integration tests for capability validation, crash behavior, upgrade scenarios, and fork prevention logic.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Extend Chaincode Shim with GetTrxState API",
      "activity_description": "Add GetTrxState(key string) method to the chaincode shim interface; implement transient transaction write tracking to support reading uncommitted writes during active transactions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Implement Per-Transaction RYW Enable Flag",
      "activity_description": "Add per-transaction configuration flag to enable RYW; update chaincode runtime to pass the flag to the shim and enforce RYW only when explicitly enabled.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Develop RYW Tests and Documentation",
      "activity_description": "Write unit tests for GetTrxState covering uncommitted reads, disabled RYW behavior, and edge cases; update chaincode developer documentation to describe usage and CouchDB-only limitations.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Create Org Addition Training Slide Deck",
      "activity_description": "Design .ppt slide deck illustrating network topology before/after org addition, config transaction flow, and pre/post verification steps for administrators.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Record Org Addition Walkthrough Video",
      "activity_description": "Record, edit, and caption 5-minute video demonstrating the step-by-step process of adding an organization to a running Fabric network without downtime.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Write Org Addition Written Guide",
      "activity_description": "Create accompanying step-by-step written guide with command examples, config snippets, and troubleshooting tips for network administrators.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "Set Up CouchDB Performance Test Environment",
      "activity_description": "Provision Fabric network with CouchDB state database; deploy benchmark chaincode with query workloads for performance testing.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A13",
      "activity_name": "Execute CouchDB Query Performance Tests",
      "activity_description": "Run controlled performance tests with varying concurrent load (10/100/1000 transactions) to measure query latency (p50/p95) and throughput.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A14",
      "activity_name": "Generate CouchDB Performance Report",
      "activity_description": "Analyze test results, document performance metrics, and provide recommendations for CouchDB deployment sizing and query optimization.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A15",
      "activity_name": "Define MSPConfig Interface and Refactor Existing Code",
      "activity_description": "Convert concrete MSPConfig type to an interface in the channelconfig API; refactor all existing dependent code to use the interface to avoid breaking changes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A16",
      "activity_name": "Implement Default MSPConfig and Update configtxgen",
      "activity_description": "Implement default MSPConfig that matches existing configtxgen behavior; update configtxgen tool to use the default implementation to preserve existing functionality.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A17",
      "activity_name": "Develop MSPConfig Interface Tests and Documentation",
      "activity_description": "Write unit tests for the interface covering custom implementation support and default implementation parity; update documentation to describe custom MSPConfig usage for external config generation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 7
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A18",
      "activity_name": "Audit and Identify Chaincode Singletons",
      "activity_description": "Review existing chaincode implementation to identify all global singletons (e.g., metadata caches, deployment singletons) that hinder testability and lifecycle management.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A19",
      "activity_name": "Refactor Chaincode Singletons to Instance-Scoped",
      "activity_description": "Refactor identified singletons to be instance-scoped; update all dependent code to use instance references, ensuring no changes to external chaincode shim API or behavior.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A20",
      "activity_name": "Update Tests for Singleton Removal",
      "activity_description": "Modify existing unit and integration tests to reflect instance-scoped chaincode; add new tests to verify correct instance isolation and no behavioral regressions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A21",
      "activity_name": "Define World Test Config Struct",
      "activity_description": "Create World struct in the Fabric test framework with fields mapping to all existing peer core.yaml and orderer.yaml configuration parameters.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A22",
      "activity_name": "Implement YAML Config Generation from World Struct",
      "activity_description": "Implement template logic to generate valid peer core.yaml and orderer.yaml files from World struct values; integrate with existing test setup code.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A23",
      "activity_name": "Develop Config Generation Tests",
      "activity_description": "Write tests to verify generated YAML matches expected values for a range of World config inputs, ensuring no config parameters are missing or misformatted.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A24",
      "activity_name": "Define Lifecycle Validation Parameters Interface",
      "activity_description": "Design and implement interface in the new chaincode lifecycle system to return validation parameters (endorsement policy, version, etc.) for chaincodes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A25",
      "activity_name": "Implement +Lifecycle Validation Edge Case",
      "activity_description": "Implement special case for the +lifecycle system chaincode to return an automatically generated majority endorsement policy as its validation info.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A26",
      "activity_name": "Add Channel Config Policy Endorsement Stub",
      "activity_description": "Implement stub functionality to support evaluating channel config policies as endorsement policies in the future, as specified in the requirement.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A27",
      "activity_name": "Develop Lifecycle Validation Interface Tests",
      "activity_description": "Write unit and integration tests for the validation interface covering regular chaincode validation, the +lifecycle edge case, and the future policy extension stub.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 194
  }
}

